{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgY217gf32cVgqyrrWk99","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Your answers are in, and the three recommended dials stand as assumed. This is the playback. It covers the reading only, and nothing is written until the next step.\n\n**What the board answers:** which screens a Fernhouse customer passes through to start a return, and where they choose. The reader is the product and design team, who use it to check the return path against the app. Settings: Balanced detail, Mixed audience, Laptop distance.\n\n**What each source settled** (the app and the returns doc, both current behavior):\n- The screens, in the order the request lists them: order list, order detail, reasons, drop-off or courier choice, confirmation.\n- The 30-day window, with Contact support after it.\n- The screen details: items with price and delivery date, the Start a return button under the items, the four reasons, the map of 5 nearest points, the date within 3 working days, the QR code and the email.\n\n**Outline**\n1. Which screens does a customer pass through to start a return, and where do they choose?\n2. Nodes, 9 in all, none cut by the remove test:\n   - Order list: entry, the start.\n   - Order detail: a screen, with a body of price, delivery date and the button under the items.\n   - Within 30 days of delivery?: a decision.\n   - Contact support: an end, drawn beside the main row.\n   - Return reason: a screen, with the four reasons as its body.\n   - Drop-off or courier pickup?: a decision.\n   - Drop-off point: a screen, with the map of 5 nearest points as its body.\n   - Courier pickup: a screen, with a date within the next 3 working days as its body.\n   - Confirmation: the goal, with the QR code and the email as its body.\n3. Edges, 9 in all, in the order the sources list them:\n   - Order list to order detail.\n   - Order detail to the window check.\n   - Window check to Return reason (Yes) and to Contact support (No).\n   - Return reason to the method choice.\n   - Method choice to Drop-off point (Drop-off point) and to Courier pickup (Courier pickup).\n   - Drop-off point to Confirmation, and Courier pickup to Confirmation.\n\nI cut the merge dot, because two arrows into Confirmation join without it. That keeps the count at 9.\n\n**Two framings**\n- **Path with branches beside it (recommended):** the main row runs from order list to confirmation, with Contact support and the method branch set beside it. It reads fastest for a team checking the path, and it shows no per-screen error states.\n- **State map:** every screen with every exit. It shows more, but it adds exits the sources do not state.\n\n**The look, all proposed**\n- **Accent:** the 30-day decision, \"late returns go to support\", because it is the one rule that sends a customer away.\n- **Zones:** Find the order (order list, order detail), Check and choose (window check, Contact support, reason, method choice) and Hand over (drop-off point, courier pickup, confirmation).\n- **Title:** Start a return.\n- **Subtitle:** From the order list to a confirmed return, for the product and design team.\n- **Source line:** Sources: the Fernhouse app and the returns doc. Left out: free pickup over 100 euros, a proposal under review.\n\n**Assumed, with what settles each**\n- **Reader:** the product and design team. You settle it by naming another reader.\n- **Where Contact support appears:** the sources say only that the app shows it after 30 days. I put the check right after the order detail, where the Start a return button would otherwise be. You settle it by telling me which screen shows Contact support.\n- **Moves between screens:** I took them from the order the request lists them in and put no trigger labels on them, apart from the decision exits.\n\nNo Brief row is left unasked.\n\nIs this reading right, or do you want to correct any row, including where Contact support appears?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2247,"cache_read_input_tokens":88617,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2247},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9fba50a8-a43f-4e3a-a625-14259e318d5a","uuid":"a2055246-8cf3-4ff1-a389-8fbfc5de56a2","timestamp":"2026-10-30T07:22:00.536Z","request_id":"req_011CgY217PJvABzKk5hocV5E"}
